WEBVTT

00:00:28.746 --> 00:00:30.871
performance and decision making.

00:00:30.913 --> 00:00:34.162
TB: It creates an invisible tax
of resentment and frustration.

00:00:34.162 --> 00:00:37.537
The more frustrated we are,
the more silent we are likely to be.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.829
And the more silent we are,

00:00:38.871 --> 00:00:40.954
the less we may be able
to do our best work.

00:00:40.996 --> 00:00:44.246
The good news, though,
is bias is not inevitable.

00:00:44.287 --> 00:00:47.204
[The Way We Work]

00:00:48.287 --> 00:00:50.996
TB: So here’s how to disrupt
bias in three steps.

00:00:50.996 --> 00:00:54.329
The first step is to create
a shared vocabulary.

00:00:54.371 --> 00:00:57.454
Sometimes bias shows up in big,
embarrassing gaffes,

00:00:57.454 --> 00:01:01.162
but more often it comes out in the little
words and phrases we choose,